er 13th)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316602141/","description":"Good day everyone,\n\nPlease join us for a fun, interactive and enjoyable evening at this wonderful, cozy Firkin Pub location to play some absolute classics like ***pictionary, scattegories, monopoly, clue, cards against humanity, taboo, jenga, hedbanz, euchre, scrabble, balderash, tapple, chess, checker, battleship and always some great new games too!***\n\n\\*Bring along your own games too if you like!\n\n\\*Joined by my other social groups too; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out with lots of friendly peers to begin our weekend with!\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we are in the back dining area to find us)**\n\n*\\*You can also ask the wait staff or bartender if you like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's games event)*\n\n**-Free Parking found on residential side streets**\n\n(Event Details Below)\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host )\n\nEvent Details:\n**The Friday Night Mix, Mingle and Games!**\n\n-A chance to play some interactive games we love like ***pictionary, scattergories, taboo, cards against humanity, jenga, monopoly, clue, euchre, scrabble, balderash, tapples, card games,and so many other choices as well!***\n\n\\*Feel free to bring your own games and friends too if you like\n-You'll find it's a cozy, relaxed and enjoyable environment!\n\n***\n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars (Cash only at the door) (HST included)\nor by e transfer: **steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n\n***\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n-Arrive any time after 7:00 pm (in the back area- great for board games, card games and mingling) (event goes to roughly 11:00 pm)\n\n\\*Great dinner menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer minimum upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\nhttps://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/\n\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)","startDate":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1999 Avenue Rd, North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎶 Niagara Falls Concert Road Trip: Roch Voisine at OLG Stage! $50 total","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316750115/","description":"# 🎶 Niagara Falls Concert Road Trip: Roch Voisine at OLG Stage!\n\n**Friday, November 13, 2026**\nReady for a night of great music and a little Niagara Falls adventure? Join us for a road trip from Toronto to see **Roch Voisine – The Lightfoot Sessions Live** at the **OLG Stage at Fallsview Casino**! 🎤🎶\n\n### 🎵 The Concert\n\nRoch Voisine brings **The Lightfoot Sessions Live** to Niagara Falls for a special evening celebrating his incredible career and the music of Canadian legend **Gordon Lightfoot**.\nVoisine is one of Canada's best-known singer-songwriters, with a career spanning four decades and 25 albums. His massive breakthrough came with *Hélène*, which went triple platinum in Canada and diamond in France.\nThe show will feature Roch's greatest hits along with his tribute to Gordon Lightfoot. 🇨🇦🎶\n**Concert:** Roch Voisine – The Lightfoot Sessions Live\n**Date:** Friday, November 13, 2026\n**Venue:** OLG Stage at Fallsview Casino\n**Showtime:** 8:00 PM\n👉 **Official show information:**\n[https://fallsviewcasinoresort.com/events-and-promotions/schedule-of-events/roch-voisine.html](https://fallsviewcasinoresort.com/events-and-promotions/schedule-of-events/roch-voisine.html)\n\n### 🚗 The Road Trip\n\nWe'll meet **outside Christie Station at 4:30 PM** and head to Niagara Falls in a **Kia Soul with SiriusXM radio**.\nDepending on traffic and how the evening is going, we may have some time to **sightsee around Niagara Falls before the concert**. 🌊📸\nAfter the show, we'll head back to Toronto.\n**Expected return to Toronto: around 11:30 PM**, depending on traffic and the timing of the evening.\n\n### 💰 COST: JUST $50\n\n**$50 includes:**\n\n* 🎟️ Your concert ticket\n* 🚗 Round-trip transportation from Toronto\n* ⛽ Transportation costs\n\nThat's it — **just $50 for the concert AND the ride!**\n\n### 📲 RESERVE YOUR SPOT\n\nSpots are **very limited** because we're travelling in a Kia Soul.\nTo reserve your spot, send **$50 by e-transfer to:**\nnicolasbello@yahoo.com\n\nYour spot is only locked in once the e-transfer has been received.\n\n### 🍁 Come for the concert. Stay for the road trip.\n\nLet's make a night of it — great music, Niagara Falls, SiriusXM on the drive, and a fun Meetup road trip with a small group!\n\n**Friday, November 13 • 4:30 PM departure • Christie Station**\n🎶 **Roch Voisine + Niagara Falls + Road Trip = Friday night plans!**","startDate":"2026-11-13T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Christie Station Labyrinth","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Christie, 5 Christie St, Toronto, ON M6G 3B1, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Koerner Hall:  Bela Fleck (19 Grammy Awards)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/316232032/","description":"**The banjo visionary leads an all‑star ensemble through some new music and classic tunes, blending bluegrass roots with jazz and classical influences.**\n\nWe have a 15% off promo code--*at the TICKET link below. Join us at Koerner Hall in mid-November!*\n\nYouTube teaser (with his All-Star band)\\*\\* The Flecktones.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6wQ3dAg_cpQ&t=17s\n\nOver the last four decades, Béla Fleck has made a point of boldly going where no banjo player has gone before, a musical journey that has earned him 19 Grammys in nine different fields, including country, pop, jazz, instrumental, classical, and global music.\n\nBut his roots are in bluegrass, and that is where he returns with his band of all-star players, My Bluegrass Heart.\n\nhttps://www.belafleck.com/\n\nTaking its namesake from Fleck's 2021 Grammy Award-winning album, *My Bluegrass Heart*, the album was the third chapter of a trilogy which began with the 1988 album, *Drive*, and continued in 1991 with The Bluegrass Sessions. Fleck’s band spotlights a multi-generational gamut of the best of bluegrass players, all sporting a myriad of Grammy nominations, as well as gigantic piles of IBMA awards for their instruments: fiddler Michael Cleveland, mandolinist Dominick Leslie, Jeff Partin on dobro, bassist/multi-instrumentalist Mark Schatz, and Jake Stargel on guitar.\n\n**TICKET link here:**\n\nhttps://www.rcmusic.com/concert/bela-fleck-my-bluegrass-heart-444601\n\nUse this promo code for 15% tickets (with the exception of the **PURPLE** seats)\n\n**ISCULTURE15**\n\nBest pricing and seat availability is ANYWHERE on Upper Balcony! Any seat is a great seat--and the sound/view is exceptional.","startDate":"2026-11-14T00:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Royal Conservatory - Koerner Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"273 Bloor St. W., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/"},"performer":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314155032/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-11-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316441944/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-11-13T23:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Canadian Chamber Orchestra Concert at the AGO + Dinner","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/316684771/","description":"**Note: This concert is Free with General Admission and seating is limited.**\n\nOn **Friday, November 13th**, **join me for the AGO's Friday Night Series, with a Special Concert from the Canadian Chamber Orchestra.** Throughout the season, hand-picked CCO musicians will take the stage in smaller ensembles, blending bold classical masterworks, contemporary music, original compositions by our own players, and fresh, inventive arrangements of popular favourites. Each performance transforms Walker Court into a vibrant, living soundscape where art, architecture, and exhilarating live music collide for an unforgettable concert experience.    Grab a drink or snack from the Espresso Bar to enjoy during the performance! Last call is 8:15 pm.\n\nPlease note this is not a traditional orchestra experience.\n\n**COST**\nAdult: Free with General Admission ($30 or Annual Pass $40 for one year)\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes**\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me at: 5:30pm inside the entrance to the right side of the AGO at 317 Dundas St. W.**\n\n**Concert: 6 - 9pm**\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.","startDate":"2026-11-13T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"AGO","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"317 Dundas St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Experience Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/"},"performer":"Experience Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎤 Toronto Karaoke Night – Every Friday at Ace of Spades Lounge 🎶","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/events/316702866/","description":"Looking for a fun Friday night in Toronto? Join us **every Friday at 8:00 PM** for an unforgettable **Karaoke Night** at **Ace of Spades Lounge**!\nWhether you're a seasoned performer or just want to cheer on your friends, everyone is welcome. Grab the mic, sing your favorite songs, meet new people, and enjoy a night full of great energy.\n\n### What to Expect\n\n🎤 Karaoke all night long\n🍔 Delicious food and late-night bites\n🍹 Great drinks from our full bar\n🤝 Meet new people and socialize\n🎶 Fun music and an exciting atmosphere\n✨ Good vibes and unforgettable memories\nCome solo, bring a date, or gather your friends—this is one of the best ways to kick off your weekend in Toronto.\n\n**📅 Every Friday**\n**🕗 Starts at 8:00 PM**\n**📍 Ace of Spades Lounge**\n536 Manning Avenue\nToronto, ON\n\n**🎙️ Grab the mic. Be the star.**\n**Come socialize, sing, eat, drink, and have fun—we'll see you every Friday!**","startDate":"2026-11-14T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ace of Spades","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"536 Manning Ave., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/"},"performer":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"(Port Credit Arena) Improv Acting Drop-In","url":"https://www.meetup.com/mississauga-improv-meetup-self-improv-ment/events/316766370/","description":"**Directions to the Room (NEW ROOM, SAME ARENA):**\nTo find the room, once in Port Credit Arena at the main entrance, go up the stairs, go through the double doors next to the washrooms and on the right you will find a room labelled John Holland.\n**Age: 18+**\n**Event Description:**\nThis is an informal improv workshop where we get together to play games and scenes similar to those in Whose Line is it Anyways: https://youtu.be/KF3D2TMUhN8. If you want to boost your acting chops or are just looking for some silly fun, this is the place to be!\nThere are usually 10-20 people. The session starts with introductions, followed by group games then finishes with audience/performance sessions. Max capacity is 30 and spots are held based on how soon you sign up. See you there!\n**Payment**\nThe price is $10 per person (interac only!) to help cover the costs of running the event. I can only accept interac e-transfer since at Mississauga facilities I'm not allowed to take cash.\n\nWe start by 7:10 please make sure to come on time.\nP.S - We usually grab dinner/drinks at one of Port Credit's fabulous nearby bars or restaurants after the session. Everyone's welcome!","startDate":"2026-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Port Credit Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"40 Stavebank Rd, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Self Improv-ment: Mississauga Improv Practice","url":"https://www.meetup.com/mississauga-improv-meetup-self-improv-ment/"},"performer":"Self Improv-ment: Mississauga Improv Practice"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/events/316784345/","description":"### **Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)**\n\n* **6:00 PM - 7:00 PM:** Pickleball Dink & Strategy Clinic (GTA Pickleball Lessons)\n* **7:00 PM - 8:00 PM (Optional):** Extra hour of game play available for an extra $5 per person. (Note: The optional extra hour (7-8 PM) requires at least 4 players to agree and depends on court availability. Please let me know early if you are interested!)\n\n**Are you ready to elevate your pickleball game?** Join our exclusive, small-group clinic designed for players who want to move beyond just hitting hard and master the soft game. If you want to improve your dinking, court positioning, and stacking strategies, this session is perfect for you!\n\n**Meet Your Instructor** Hi, I'm Jeong, an NCCP-certified Level 2 pickleball and tennis instructor based in the GTA. I focus on helping players build solid technical fundamentals and strategic court awareness to win more rallies.\n\n**Verified Coach Profiles & Reviews**\n\n* [Superprof.ca](https://www.superprof.ca/nccp-certified-tennis-pickleball-instructor-teaching-the-basic-theory-and-practical-skills-tennis-pickl.html)\n* [Teachme.to](https://teachme.to/listings/pickleball/pickleball-with-jeong-sohn?skill=pickleball&latitude=43.866955&longitude=-79.440567)\n* [Playtogether.ca](https://playtogether.ca/about/)\n\n**What to Expect (60-Minute Session):**\n\n* **Warm-up & Assessment:** Quick rallies to assess your current level and identify key areas for improvement.\n* **Core Skills Training:** Step-by-step drills focusing on dink consistency, tactical positioning, and an introduction to stacking strategies.\n* **Guided Match Play:** Apply what you've learned in organized mini-games with real-time, personalized feedback.\n\n**Event Details:**\n\n* **Location:** Swing Star (5 Connie Crescent Unit 1, Vaughan, ON)\n* **Date & Time:** Every (Fri) 6-7pm\n* **Skill Level:** Beginner to Low-Intermediate\n* **Spots Available:** Strictly limited to 6-8 players to ensure quality coaching.\n* **Fee:** $20 (Covers court usage, practice balls, and instruction).\n* **Min-Max** Students: 3-6 (If there are fewer than 3 registrations, the amount paid via PayPal will be refunded via e-Transfer)\n* **Optional Extra Hour**: If you'd like to stay and play games after the 6-7 PM lesson, an additional hour (7-8 PM) is available for just **$5 per person**. This option is available if at least 4 players stay!","startDate":"2026-11-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Swing Star - Indoor Golf And Pickleball","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Vaughan","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1-15 Connie Crescent,, Vaughan, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/"},"performer":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/d/3/3/highres_536187955.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/6/9/1/highres_536358065.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/a/3/highres_451449891.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/7/6/d/highres_527105997.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/8/2/4/highres_510374372.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/f/6/b/highres_536283947.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https